adjudication.rationale:
In `packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/workflows.tsx` (the activeOn-disable path around `//cancel workflow reminders for all bookings from event types that got disabled`), the previous DB deletes were collected and awaited (`await Promise.all(deleteReminderPromise)`), but the new code only calls the async managers inside `forEach` without `await` or promise collection:
```ts
remindersToDelete.flat().forEach((reminder) => {
  if (reminder.method === WorkflowMethods.EMAIL) {
    deleteScheduledEmailReminder(reminder.id, reminder.referenceId);
  } else if (...) {
    deleteScheduledSMSReminder(reminder.id, reminder.referenceId);
  }
});
```
Both `deleteScheduledEmailReminder` and `deleteScheduledSMSReminder` are `async` (see their definitions in the diff), so DB updates/deletes (and Twilio cancels for SMS) are not awaited and may not complete before the resolver finishes, especially in serverless/process-recycle scenarios. (Note: the finding’s mention of “SendGrid cancels” in this path is overstated because EMAIL now defaults to DB-flagging unless `immediateDelete` is passed, but the unawaited async work is still a real defect.)
